From 976144eb6285be02cde3de42ab251dc2875ae43a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 05:44:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] P7-printing-module-product-aggregate-integration

Printing Module, Phase 7 (ProductService wired to the composer - the module's original
requirement finally holds end to end: product and print configuration behave as one
aggregate). Three confirmed decisions locked this phase's shape:

1. Attaching a print-config payload at product creation is system-admin only; creating a
   PLAIN product (no config) stays open to any tenant caller - only the combined action is
   gated, not product creation itself.
2. UsingPrinterType removed entirely from UpdateProductRequest. A product's printer family can
   now change only via PUT /api/products/{id}/print-config (system-admin only, atomic switch
   per Q-08) - never independently through the plain product update. Two code paths capable of
   changing the same field was the risk being closed here.
3. GET /api/products/{id} stays untouched (no interface change) - print config remains reachable
   via its own endpoint. Added instead: GET /api/products/{id}/print-config/full, system-admin
   only, returning product + print config combined in one call (PrintConfig is null, not an
   error, when the product has none yet - an admin overview should work at any lifecycle stage).

Changes:
- CreateProductRequest: gained optional Matica/Evolis fields. ProductService.CreateAsync
  validates via the composer before opening a transaction (a bad payload never creates the
  product either), then stages both inside one ExecuteInTransactionAsync - passing the Product
  entity itself to StageForProductAsync (P6's fix), not a bare id, since product.Id doesn't
  exist until that same SaveChanges call runs.
- UpdateProductRequest: UsingPrinterType field removed (not just ignored - removed from the
  contract, so the API honestly reflects what's possible).
- ProductService.SoftDeleteAsync / RestoreAsync: moved from a bare SaveChangesAsync to
  ExecuteInTransactionAsync, cascading to IProductPrintConfigComposer.SoftDeleteForProductAsync /
  RestoreForProductAsync in the same commit as the product's own soft-delete/restore.
- ProductPrintConfigurationService: new GetProductWithConfigAsync (system-admin only, bypasses
  tenant scope). BuildResponseAsync refactored into a shared TryBuildConfigResponseAsync used by
  both GetForProductAsync (fails when no config exists) and GetProductWithConfigAsync (tolerates
  none). ProductResponse mapping duplicated as a single trivial line rather than reaching into
  ProductService - services in this codebase are siblings talking to repositories, not to
  each other.
- ProductPrintConfigController: new GET api/products/{id}/print-config/full.
- PrintingErrors.ProductPrintConfigOnlySystemAdmin wording generalized ('create or update',
  was 'update') since the same code now covers both paths - EN + AR resx updated to match, no
  new key needed.

Cleanup: removed CreateProductPrintConfigRequest (ApplicationLayer/DTOs/Printing/PrintingDtos.cs),
defined in P2 but never consumed - P7 bypassed it by flattening Matica/Evolis directly onto
CreateProductRequest instead of nesting them under a second, redundant UsingPrinterType field
that could disagree with the product's own. Dead code, removed rather than left stale.

Verified: no other Product entity construction site exists outside ProductService (checked
before touching it); IProductService is the only interface ProductService implements, with no
other implementers to break; every composer/repo call cross-checked against its real contract
signature; DTO field order cross-checked constructor-call to record-definition for every new or
changed type; 27/27 error codes still have full EN/AR resx parity after the wording edit.
